course: dictionary
lesson: 44
title: Accidental: by chance, not on purpose
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Accidental means happening by chance, not planned or meant. The word has «accident» inside it, and an accident is something that happens by mistake. «Reading your work aloud is the quickest way to hear an accidental tense slip.» A tense slip is a mistake, and nobody plans a mistake, so accidental fits here.
explain: «Turning off a saved card means the full card number must be typed in, which stops accidental buys.» Think about what the card rule stops: buys that happen by mistake, not buys someone chose. Try your meaning in the sentence: "stops buys made by mistake" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: The same idea works in other phrases. An accidental fall is a fall nobody planned, and accidental damage is harm done by mistake. In music, though, accidental is a special word for a sharp or flat added to a note, so always check the subject you are reading about.
fact: Accidental means happening by chance, not planned or meant.
fact: Accidental is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a fall, a slip or a buy.
fact: Useful phrases: accidental damage, accidental discovery, purely accidental.
fact: In music, an accidental is a sign such as a sharp or flat added to a note.
fact: In formal writing, accidental can also mean not essential or not part of the main thing.
exercise: «Turning off a saved card stops accidental buys.» What does accidental mean here? | Done again and again | Planned and carefully chosen | *Made by mistake, not on purpose | Very expensive
exercise: What is an accidental discovery? | A discovery kept secret | *A discovery made by chance | A discovery planned for years | A discovery that nobody wanted
exercise: In music, what is an accidental? | *A sharp or a flat added to a note | A word that means happening by chance | A question mark | A comma
test: Which word means happening by chance, not planned? | Essential | *Accidental | Careful | Planned
test: «Reading your work aloud is the quickest way to hear an accidental tense slip.» What is an accidental tense slip? | A planned change of tense | *A mistake made without meaning to | A long, sad story | A game played with tenses
exam: Which phrase describes accidental damage? | *Harm done by mistake | A happy surprise | Harm done on purpose | A planned repair
